WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:09.100
One of the hardest things for a human to comprehend
is the idea of an end.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:16.219
The idea of our existence ending and not having
the slightest definitive clue as to where

00:00:16.219 --> 00:00:20.119
it may or may not go.

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:25.260
How we can fall in love with life and all
the things within it.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:29.660
How we can feel so strongly about our passions
and careers.

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:37.780
And how we can analyze, appreciate, and mend
the features of our identity, all for it just

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:42.309
to end and dissolve into the ether.

00:00:42.309 --> 00:00:49.719
Like all living organisms, as soon as we are
born, we begin our journey towards death.

00:00:49.719 --> 00:00:56.559
We travel through life with our finite timeline
hovering over us, forced to live with the

00:00:56.559 --> 00:01:04.780
increasing pressure of only having so much
time to decide what to do with time itself.

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:10.690
When we are young, we don’t think or worry
about this so much.

00:01:10.690 --> 00:01:18.150
Our consciousness is not yet developed enough
to consider the concept of life and death.

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:24.970
But as we get older and step more and more
into our consciousness, we begin to grasp

00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:32.640
the shortness and complexity of life as we
realize that our parents and teachers no longer

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:39.590
have all the answers to our increasingly critical
questions of life.

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:47.600
And interestingly, simultaneous to our developing
realization of this, our life becomes filled

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:53.370
with increasing amounts of work and responsibility.

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:59.550
As a child, we go from hanging around at home,
to having to go to school.

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:06.540
And as we progress through school, each grade
becomes slightly harder and more time consuming

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:09.460
than the previous.

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:16.580
Then we go from high school to college or
a career and then hopefully to success, as

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:23.970
we might define it, each stage requiring more
and more of our time and energy.

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:32.019
It appears that as we become closer and more
aware of life’s approaching end, life requires

00:02:32.019 --> 00:02:35.040
more and more from us.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:41.690
But why is it that we are willing to invest
increasing amounts of time and energy into

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:46.560
a life that we are getting closer and closer
to losing?

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:53.959
Why work our life away in pursuit of goals
and achievements for them to most likely just

00:02:53.959 --> 00:02:58.159
dissolve away with us when we die.

00:02:58.159 --> 00:03:00.480
The reason is simple.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:07.870
We strive for purpose, achievement, and wealth,
beyond just our survival needs, because it

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:15.700
distracts us from thinking about this very
idea of our mortality in a healthy and sustainable

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:16.910
way.

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:23.299
What’s worse than to live and work towards
something that doesn’t ultimately matter

00:03:23.299 --> 00:03:30.909
to the universe, is to live a life having
done nothing but sit with fear and sadness.

00:03:30.909 --> 00:03:35.650
To waste the experience on inactivity.

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:41.370
If we do not work towards goals and dreams,
we will have nothing to focus on and all of

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:45.680
our unutilized time and energy will divert
towards destructive habits in an attempt to

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:51.120
occupy our mind away from thinking about death
and futility.

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:58.180
Purpose and success is arguably nothing more
than a human construct designed to distract

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:05.359
us from the fact that we are only conscious
enough to create and achieve, but not conscious

00:04:05.359 --> 00:04:10.139
enough to understand the point of any of it.

00:04:10.139 --> 00:04:17.630
To acquire true purpose and success in life
is not necessarily to achieve wealth, fame,

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:26.010
or status, but to feel the passion and vitality
that comes from working towards goals and

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:27.010
dreams.

00:04:27.010 --> 00:04:33.919
To be happily distracted away from worrying
about life’s complexity and shortness.

00:04:33.919 --> 00:04:43.210
In life, we play video games, board games,
sports games etc. not because they go on forever,

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:49.020
but because they are fun and engage our capacity
to feel human.

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:54.699
We play them because they help us forget about
the reality of life’s impermanence.

00:04:54.699 --> 00:05:01.800
And because we need the feeling of having
some participation in the collective happenings

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:05.710
around us in order to feel happy and alive.

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:10.880
And the game of life itself is no different.

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:14.229
By nature, we are all competitive beings.

00:05:14.229 --> 00:05:22.550
And to not work, contribute, and feel involved
is to feel unimportant and lesser than our

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:24.810
fellow humans.

00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:31.520
And there are few things that kill a soul
quicker than the feeling of inferiority and

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:32.520
insignificance.

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:34.440
Even more so than the realization of the absurdity
of the game itself.

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:38.400
Ultimately we are left with two choices in
life.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:06:13.629
Play and enjoy the game as best we can, or
stay on the sidelines and complain about 

00:06:13.629 --> 00:06:14.750
the rules.

